%N A322653 Numbers that are sums of one or more consecutive octagonal pyramidal numbers (A002414).
%C A322653 The first term that occurs in more than one way is a(59) = 3180 = Sum_{k=3 .. 10} A002414(k) = Sum_{k=11 .. 12} A002414(k). - _Robert Israel_, Aug 05 2026
%H A322653 Robert Israel, <a href="/A322653/b322653.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A322653 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PyramidalNumber.html">Pyramidal Number</a>
%p A322653 ops:= [seq(k*(3*k - 1)*(k + 2)*(k + 1)/12,k=0..40)]:
%p A322653 M = ops[-1]-ops[-2]:
%p A322653 S:= select(`<=`,{0,seq(seq(ops[i]-ops[j],j=1..i-1),i=1..40)},M):
%p A322653 sort(convert(S,list)); # _Robert Israel_, Aug 05 2026
%Y A322653 Cf. A002414, A002419, A320728, A321450, A322468, A322479, A322637, A322651, A322652.
